---
// Naive attention: three kernels, and the big N×N matrices S and P travel through HBM.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 720 330" role="img" aria-label="Naive attention runs three kernels. The first reads Q and K and writes the full score matrix S to HBM. The second reads S and writes P. The third reads P and V and writes the output O. S and P are 134 MB each per head at 8K tokens.">
  <defs>
    <marker id="fan-r" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="t3" /></marker>
    <marker id="fan-w" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="tr" /></marker>
  </defs>
  <!-- lanes -->
  <rect x="8" y="34" width="704" height="100" rx="12" class="box2" style="opacity:0.6" />
  <text x="20" y="54" class="t3 mono" font-size="10.5">ON THE CHIP (SRAM / registers): fast, small</text>
  <rect x="8" y="182" width="704" height="100" rx="12" class="box2" style="opacity:0.6" />
  <text x="20" y="276" class="t3 mono" font-size="10.5">HBM: big, but every trip costs time</text>

  <!-- kernels -->
  <rect x="70" y="66" width="160" height="54" rx="10" class="box-a" />
  <text x="150" y="88" class="ta mono" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle">KERNEL 1</text>
  <text x="150" y="107" class="t" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">S = Q·Kᵀ</text>
  <rect x="280" y="66" width="160" height="54" rx="10" class="box-a" />
  <text x="360" y="88" class="ta mono" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle">KERNEL 2</text>
  <text x="360" y="107" class="t" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">P = softmax(S)</text>
  <rect x="490" y="66" width="160" height="54" rx="10" class="box-a" />
  <text x="570" y="88" class="ta mono" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle">KERNEL 3</text>
  <text x="570" y="107" class="t" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">O = P·V</text>

  <!-- HBM tensors -->
  <rect x="24" y="196" width="50" height="40" rx="6" class="box" /><text x="49" y="221" class="t mono" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Q</text>
  <rect x="84" y="196" width="50" height="40" rx="6" class="box" /><text x="109" y="221" class="t mono" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">K</text>
  <rect x="160" y="192" width="150" height="62" rx="6" class="red" /><text x="235" y="218" class="tr mono" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">S  (N × N)</text><text x="235" y="238" class="tr mono" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle">134 MB</text>
  <rect x="330" y="192" width="150" height="62" rx="6" class="red" /><text x="405" y="218" class="tr mono" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">P  (N × N)</text><text x="405" y="238" class="tr mono" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle">134 MB</text>
  <rect x="510" y="196" width="50" height="40" rx="6" class="box" /><text x="535" y="221" class="t mono" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">V</text>
  <rect x="610" y="196" width="50" height="40" rx="6" class="box" /><text x="635" y="221" class="t mono" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">O</text>

  <!-- reads (grey, up) and writes (red, down) -->
  <path d="M49 196 L110 124" class="line-t" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#fan-r)" />
  <path d="M109 196 L135 124" class="line-t" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#fan-r)" />
  <path d="M195 120 L225 188" class="sr" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#fan-w)" />
  <path d="M260 192 L315 124" class="line-t" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#fan-r)" />
  <path d="M400 120 L410 188" class="sr" stroke-width="1.8" marker-end="url(#fan-w)" />
  <path d="M440 192 L520 124" class="line-t" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#fan-r)" />
  <path d="M535 196 L555 124" class="line-t" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#fan-r)" />
  <path d="M615 120 L632 192" class="line-a" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#fan-w)" />

  <text x="20" y="306" class="t2" font-size="11.5">One head, N = 8,192 tokens, BF16: Q, K, V and O are about 2.1 MB each, but S and P are about 134 MB each.</text>
  <text x="20" y="324" class="t2" font-size="11.5">Writing and reading them back moves about <tspan class="tr mono" font-weight="700">537 MB</tspan> through HBM for one head of one layer.</text>
</svg>
